-q, [ \"$(...)\" -eq N ], jq -e) so a failure is observable"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State AC5's behavior when the SSM probe channel itself fails (SendCommand timeout / host unreachable / IAM denial): treat it as a non-zero-exit failure distinct from the device-not-reported UNKNOWN outcome, so a transport failure never yields a passing result.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.851,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'It joins the two halves nobody had joined -- terraform's aws_volume_attachment set against the host's mount table'","Three outcomes named: UNKNOWN ('host did not report the device'), NOT-IN-SERVICE, in-service — none covers SSM-channel/transport failure","AC3 notes a real 'probe-truncation defect' on this host that can make a probe 'go blind', implying transport-level failure is a live risk"],"finding":"AC5's probe (`assert_volumes_in_service.py`) reads the host mount table via SSM, but the plan specifies behavior only for the device-level outcomes (in-service / NOT-IN-SERVICE / UNKNOWN 'host did not report the device'). It does not state what the script does when the SSM channel itself fails (SendCommand timeout, host unreachable, IAM denial) — distinct from a device the host simply didn't report.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3fcb409068c0bfeb","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC5 (`scripts/assert_volumes_in_service.py`) and Verification section","norm_id":"nd669e34467e8c382","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future `terraform apply` runs the mandatory post-apply probe while the SSM agent is down or the invoking role lacks ssm:SendCommand — the script must fail loudly rather than exit 0 or hang","The probe-truncation defect truncates the SSM command output"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a fourth explicit outcome (or fold into a fail-closed rule): if the host cannot be probed at all, exit non-zero with a 'PROBE-FAILED' message naming the instance, rather than reporting in-service or exiting 0.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] In AC5, explicitly scope the new script to the Terraform aws_volume_attachment join/auto-discovery delta and justify re-implementing host mount-state classification in Python instead of composing with the existing infra/scripts/check-mounts.sh (which already applies the same three-outcome discipline).","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["infra/scripts/check-mounts.sh:40-44 documents 'THREE outcomes, not two: mounted (0), not mounted (1), and CANNOT TELL (2)' — the same discipline the new classify() re-derives","tests/unit/test_assert_volumes_in_service_dcc3.py:136 itself states the UNKNOWN outcome is 'the same discipline infra/scripts/check-mounts.sh applies'","AC5 text: 'It joins the two halves nobody had joined' makes no mention of check-mounts.sh","Genuine delta is documented at infra/runbooks/gate-scratch-mount.md:312-314: check-mounts.sh uses a hardcoded mount-set ('written per-volume in three places... A third volume gets no metric... until someone adds them by hand'), which the Terraform-attachment join removes"],"finding":"AC5 presents the host mount-state classification as novel ('the two halves nobody had joined') without acknowledging the existing infra/scripts/check-mounts.sh, which already implements the identical three-outcome host mount-state discipline (mounted / not-mounted / cannot-tell) that the new script re-derives in Python (parse_host_mounts/classify). The genuinely new capability is only the Terraform aws_volume_attachment join / auto-discovery of the expected set; the plan should scope the new code to that delta and justify re-implementing host-side classification rather than composing with the existing probe.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0dcd602409d14b25","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC5 (scripts/assert_volumes_in_service.py)","norm_id":"n1dd94fbabd5a2e03","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future maintainer changing mount-state semantics must now keep check-mounts.sh (host-side) and assert_volumes_in_service.py (control-plane) in agreement, with the classification logic duplicated across shell and Python"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to AC5 acknowledging check-mounts.sh and stating the boundary: the new script owns ONLY the terraform-attachment-set discovery + join (removing the hardcoded per-volume list check-mounts.sh maintains), while the host-side mount verdict is either delegated to check-mounts.sh over SSM or, if reparsed in Python for the serial-based join, called out as an intentional (tested) mirror of check-mounts.sh's classification.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State, in the plan (not only the delegated runbook), the transition-safety of the live data move: how gate admission (and the review-bot clone path) is quiesced/refusing during copy+cutover so no writes land on root between snapshot and mount, and the partial-failure/back-out behavior of the AC4 reclaim delete.","cohort":["T11"],"criteria":["T11"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: '/var/lib/rebar/gate-scratch held LIVE working directories, so mounting over them would HIDE them while stranding the bytes on root.'","AC4: 'The stranded copy under root is reclaimed and df / reflects it' — a delete/reclaim step with no stated back-out or partial-failure handling.","The safe copy-then-cutover-then-reclaim ordering lives in 'infra/runbooks/gate-scratch-mount.md', which is named but NOT included in the plan text, so the dual-write-window and reclaim-failure handling are unknowable from the material under review.","The follow-up sibling ticket already notes the review-bot clone path (voter.py) does NOT pass through gate_admission's refusal, so writers to root may not all be quiesced during the transition."],"finding":"The plan moves LIVE gate-scratch working directories onto the new volume and then deletes ('reclaims') the stranded copy on root, but it does not assert on the SAFETY of that transition: whether gate admission is quiesced/refusing while the copy and cutover happen (so no gate writes to root between snapshotting the tree and mounting over it — a lost-writes / dual-write window), nor what state results if the reclaim delete fails partway. The ordered procedure is delegated entirely to infra/runbooks/gate-scratch-mount.md, whose safety steps are not in the plan text under review.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff5aa80a329ea19b3","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC4 ('The stranded copy under root is reclaimed and df / reflects it') and the 'Why remediation was not a simple mount' section","norm_id":"n10a6bf0ef74a6a97","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A gate (or the review-bot clone path that bypasses gate_admission) writes new working-directory bytes to root AFTER the tree is copied but BEFORE the mount is placed — those writes are shadowed by the mount and then destroyed by the AC4 reclaim.","The reclaim `rm` of the stranded root copy fails or is interrupted partway, leaving root partially cleared with no stated recovery state."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to AC4 (or the 'Why remediation was not a simple mount' section) an explicit ordered guarantee: (1) put gate admission into refusal AND stop the review-bot before copying, (2) copy the live tree to the mounted volume, (3) cut over, (4) verify from inside the container, and only THEN (5) reclaim root — with the reclaim being a reversible move-aside (e.g. rename to a quarantine dir, delete after a confirmation window) rather than an immediate rm, so a partial failure leaves recoverable state.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"346b3a147424d5c0","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["439aea7a0918da78",7840],"description_boxes":["4cf0c1012276f46a",8],"file_impact":["772ef2112bf767eb",4],"ticket_id":["c04682803e6ac8ed",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":594560,"cache_write_tokens":286479,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":13011.1,"input_tokens":901739,"llm_calls":28,"llm_ms":212341.7,"output_tokens":28259,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":255706.2,"verify_requests":11},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","priority_floor":0.8,"provider_provenance":{"candidates":["